title.narrative:
Measurable indicator:  •Benefit sharing trends for the transboundary PAs;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Amount of revenue (USD) received per PA plotted against time (years). Presented as either a line graph or bar graph;
As a result, there was a slight drop in revenue sharing amounts due to complete suspension of tourism in all PAs in 2021 as consequence of COVID 19 pandemic.

Measurable indicator:  Benefit sharing trends for the transboundary PAs;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:   Amount of revenue (USD) received per PA plotted against time (years) and Presented as either a line graph or bar graph.
Result: No data.

Measurable indicator:  Cross border tourism information uploaded on GVTC website for sharing                                                                                   and Advocacy engagement/dialogues held, and recommendations made for simplified visa regime in GVL partner states                
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of uploads and count of recommendations;
Result: zero (0).

Measurable indicator: Number of PA Management recommendations agreed on any contagious Pas;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of recommendations;
As a result, none because of Covid meeting restrictions.

Measurable indicator:  Number of funding partners attracted for conservation of GVL;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of funding proposals submitted and funded;
Result: 2 : Vanishing Treasures and UNEP decade of Restoration

Measurable indicator: number of joint GVL branding tourism promotion activities done with National agencies and tourist trends disaggregated by various tourism products;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation: Count of promotion activities
As a result, zero (0) joint branding. The GVTC plans to build a portal that will specifically showcase the tourism assets of the GVL and market those assets to the benefit of the three countries, their private sectors, and the communities. A consultation exercise will be conducted to this end.

Measurable indicator: Number of partners collaborating with GVTC on transboundary wildlife conservation and tourism development;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation: Count of partner MoUs;
Result: For year 2022, 30 stakeholders actively participated in GVTC activities for GVL conservation and Tourism development, especially through the GVL Stakeholders forum.

Measurable indicator: Number of recommendations agreed and implemented by the PAAs and partners; 
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of insecurity incidences; Count of times information is shared;
As a result, In Virunga National Park, gorilla tourism has not resumed due to Covid and insecurity. Even Gorilla monitoring has not been possible due to insecurity.

Measurable indicator: Number of recommendations made through RTCs that are adopted by the PAAs;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:   Count of recommendations;
Result: For year 2022, recommendations from the Regional technical Commitees adopted by the PAAs: Landscape management  9, Law enforcement 8, Community Conservation 18 and Tourism Development 16.

Measurable indicator:  Number of recommendations made through RTCs that are adopted by the PAAs;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of recommendations;
Result: zero (0). Not Implemented due to Covid-19

Measurable indicator: Number of regional and international collaborative engagements;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation: Count of engagement;
Result: 6 virtual engagements and 3 engagements (Glasscow, Dubai and CBFP in Cameroon) implementing the post 2020 global biodiversity framework;

Measurable indicator:  Number of security dialogue meetings, recommendations made and presented to relevant stakeholders for action;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Count of recommendations;
As a result, security meetings could not be held virtually since most of the discussions done under closed doors; the issues raised.

For year 2022, security dialogue meetings  didn't take place

Measurable indicator: Number of steps supported towards ratification of the treaty in each of the partner states;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation: Count of steps;
Result: Consultation with PS Ministers done. Uganda developing Cabinet paper with GVTC technical input;

For year 2023, GVTC has held briefing sessions with the Ministers in Uganda and Rwanda; GVTC contributed to the drafting of the Cabinet paper for GVTC treaty ratification. In Uganda the process is at an advance stage. In Rwanda, the cabinet paper was prepared but at the Cabinet meeting of Rwanda, the Government of Rwanda has suggested that the Summit be removed from the GVTC Governing structure, the Board has approved this move, and this is on the agenda of the forthcoming GVTC Council of Ministers.

Measurable indicator: Number of transboundary wildlife conservation legislative recommendations agreed by PAAs;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation: Count of recommendations
Result: None

Measurable indicator:  Number of visitors to the GVTC website requesting for data and or downloading it;
Description and unit of measurement and disaggregation:  Website data analysis;
Result: 53 Subscribed to GVTC Website
